                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Aquaman without face gestures [/h1] \n\n[u] Pros:[/u]\n+ Challenging game (difficult even on easy)\n+ Active development.\n\n[u] Cons:[/u]\n- Unbalanced AI\n\n[h1] Gameplay [/h1] \n\nIt seems like you lose HP for just being near an enemy since there is almost no attack coming from any of them (maybe there is no animation at all). Also, when the character attacks he doesn't move from his position.\n\nYou are not supposed to fall from the ground but some stages can trigger this if you get too close to some edges(the character automatically climbs some).\n\n [b]Difficulty and AI[/b]\nThere is a little problem when it comes to fighting bosses in this game. It is almost impossible to defeat them without abusing of certain aspects of the character like the \"mana\" (or resource to use skills). Same happens with most of the enemies. Some can be defeated with a single combo, meanwhile, others must be dodged and attacked from far due to their high damage.\n\nI have encountered certain problems like, some enemies that become invincible. With that, some disappear after a while but others stay forever waiting for you to restart the chapter (gladly this was fixed). In fact, there was a problematic amount of core bugs that fortunately have been taken care of.\n\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1832215073\n\n\n[b]Content & Prices[/b] \nThere is almost no detailed environment and most of the time we will be limited to walk through a single path, with nothing to explore. \n\nThe game is a little bit overpriced when it comes to content. After some point, enemies are the same again and again plus you get used to similar environments. 10$ would be a more grateful price.\n\nIn terms of performance: I played the game with the following specs: i5-7400, 8GB RAM, GTX1050 Ti 4GB. The game ran perfectly at 60 fps on max settings.\n\nhttps://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1838431975\n\nA few good updates have been applied recently, improving the mechanism of the game as to how it is supposed to be (you don't wanna know how it was before).\n\n[b]Final Opinion[/b]\n\nFor a hack and slash, this game needs more action in combats(specifying, more movement) and a little bit more of explorable environment, collectibles, enemies or additional content but in general, it matches the definition of the genre.\n\n[h1][b]RATING: 7/10[/b][/h1]",
